== Description ==
Available only to the {{ClassTooltip|class_name=Abolisher}} class. Bestows a lot of different bonuses, unlocking more as it reaches higher level.

Gains [[Experience#Pet Experience|experience]] through spells only, depending on Summoning Efficiency. When {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Materialise Doppelganger}} is not assigned to a spell scroll, loses 1/3 level each second.

== Pet Abilities ==

On ability activation (every 1 second), grants 1 [[Sources|mana source]] whose cost must not exceed:
<br><math>1000 \times M</math>

From level 40, multiplies Shards Pool capacity by:
<br><math>P^{0.02} \times L^3 \times 10000 + 1</math>


From level 60, autoclicks once per 2 seconds.

From level 80, multiplies spell shards per click by:
<br><math>P^{0.25} \times L \times 0.1 + 1</math>

From level 100, multiplies spell shards per second by:
<br><math>P^{0.2} \times L \times 0.5 + 1</math>

From level 120, multiplies profits by:
<br><math>P^{0.25} \times L \times C \times 0.1 + 1</math>

From level 140, multiplies Evocation efficiency by:
<br><math>P^{0.25} \times L \times S^{0.3} \times 0.1 + 1</math>

From level 160, multiplies Incantation efficiency by:
<br><math>P^{0.1} \times L \times 0.1 + 1</math>

From level 180, multiplies Mysteries power by:
<br><math>P^{0.2} \times L \times (D + 1) + 1</math>


where:
* <math>M = \text{All Mana this Realm}</math>
* <math>P = \text{Pet Ability Power}</math>
* <math>L = \text{Pet Level}</math>
* <math>C = \text{Character Level}</math>
* <math>S = \text{Spells Cast this Exile}</math>
* <math>D = \text{Enchanting Dust Collected this Exile}</math>

== Experience Gain ==
Loses experience each second, while {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Materialise Doppelganger}} is '''not''' on the spell panel, equal to:
<br><math>\frac{N}{3}</math>

''Note: There is a 2 second buffer after removing {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Materialise Doppelganger}} before XP loss resumes.''

Accrues experience through {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Materialise Doppelganger}}. This is disbursed at a maximum rate per second, equal to:
<br><math>N \times 2</math>

where:
* <math>N = \text{Pet Experience Needed for Next Level}</math>


''Note: Doppelganger's experience needed for next level is the same as other T1 pets.''

